  "description": "DRIT.Drawing is a pure-managed, cross-platform 2D graphics library for .NET that provides a direct replacement for System.Drawing.Common. It offers comprehensive drawing capabilities for lines, shapes, arcs, polygons, and text with built-in font support for TrueType, OpenType, CFF, Type1, WOFF/WOFF2 formats. Includes a vector-first architecture with a VectorScene domain model that captures any Graphics drawing as true vector SVG or EMF/WMF/EMF+ metafile output (reading and writing), plus SVG read/write, Animated PNG (APNG), full Unicode bidirectional text (UAX #9), automatic font fallback, rich text runs, and text-on-path.",
